{"name":"Sweet Lavender","hex":"#8e8db9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Lavender","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Lavender is a play in three acts by Arthur Wing Pinero, first performed in 1888. The sentimental and gently humorous story concerns the romance of Lavender Rolt and Clement Hale, and the complications impeding the course of true love."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/86/Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Lavender"},{"title":"Sweet Lavender (1920 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Lavender is a 1920 American silent drama film directed by Paul Powell and starring Mary Miles Minter. The scenario was adapted by Beulah Marie Dix from the 1888 play of the same name by Arthur Wing Pinero. Like many of Minter's features, it is thought to be a lost film."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Sweet_Lavender_1.png/330px-Sweet_Lavender_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Lavender_(1920_film)"},{"title":"Sweetness","blocks":[{"text":"Sweetness is a basic taste most commonly perceived when eating foods rich in sugar. Sweet tastes are generally regarded as pleasurable. In addition to sugars like sucrose, many other chemical compounds are sweet, including aldehydes, ketones, and sugar alcohols. Some are sweet at very low concentrations, allowing their use as non-caloric sugar substitutes. Such non-sugar sweeteners include saccharin, aspartame, sucralose and stevia. Other compounds, such as miraculin, may alter perception of sweetness itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Strawberry_shortcake.jpg/330px-Strawberry_shortcake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetness"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/86/Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/86/Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sweet-Lavender-1922.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1922 London production of Sweet Lavender. Ann Trevor, far right, played Lavender, and Lilian Braithwaite, next to her, was Mrs Rolt.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweet-Lavender-1922.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f8/Sweet-Lavender-1888.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sweet-Lavender-1888.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.